.TH UNARC 1 "October 2026" "FreeArc 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unarc \- FreeArc high-compression archive unpacker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unarc
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIarchive\fR[\fI.arc\fR] [\fIfilenames...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unarc
is a lightweight, standalone decompression utility for FreeArc archives (.arc).
It supports testing, listing, and extracting files created with all FreeArc
compression algorithms and encryption schemes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B l
Display archive file listing.
.TP
.B v
Display verbose archive file listing with file attributes and CRCs.
.TP
.B t
Test archive integrity.
.TP
.B e
Extract files into current directory without pathnames.
.TP
.B x
Extract files with pathnames.
.TP
.B p
Extract files to standard output (pipe).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-dp \ PATH\fR,\ \fB\-d \ PATH
Set destination directory for extracted files.
.TP
.BI \-p \ PASS
Specify archive password for decryption.
.TP
.B \-o+\fR, \fB\-y
Overwrite existing files without prompting.
.TP
.B \-o-\fR, \fB\-n
Do not overwrite existing files.
.TP
.B \-s\fR, \fB\-q
Silent mode (suppress output except errors).
.TP
.BI \-x \ PATTERN
Exclude files matching pattern (@listfile supported).
.TP
.BI \-i \ PATTERN
Include only files matching pattern (@listfile supported).
.TP
.B \-so
Write extracted file contents to stdout.
.SH AUTHOR
Modern native C/C++ port by seb3773. Original FreeArc format by Bulat Ziganshin.
